+
+\item{group.by, sample.by}{Metadata columns identifying clusters and samples.
+Both must be complete. Bars show within-cluster cell fractions.}
+
+\item{features}{Marker genes in display order. Color shows population-SD
+z scores of cluster means, clipped to 0--2; size shows expressing fraction.
+Constant genes have z = 0; unmatched genes remain missing.}
+
+\item{program.by}{Metadata column containing per-cell program assignments.}
+
+\item{program.scores}{Numeric metadata columns containing program scores.
+Optional names label programs. The highest score wins; ties are Ambiguous
+and cells without finite scores are Unassigned.}
+
+\item{programs}{Named gene sets. Each gene is standardized across cells using
+population SD; the highest set mean determines assignment. At least two
+sets must meet min.program.genes.
+Supply exactly one of program.by, program.scores and programs.}
+
+\item{gsea}{A RunGSEA result or table with Groups, ID, NES and pvalue columns.
+Tidy names cluster, feature, nes and p_value are also accepted. NULL uses
+stored results for group.by and test.use. Color shows NES clipped to
+-2.5--2.5; dot area shows -ln(raw P). Missing or NOT_EVALUABLE entries
+use gray crosses.}
+
+\item{pathways}{Pathway IDs or unambiguous descriptions in display order.
+NULL shows all supplied pathways without significance filtering.}
+
+\item{db}{Value to select from the GSEA table's Database column.}
+
+\item{test.use}{Test used to locate stored RunGSEA results.}
+
+\item{class.by, subclass.by}{Metadata columns with one annotation per cluster.
+Mixed annotations require an explicit map.}
+
+\item{class.map, subclass.map}{Named cluster-to-annotation vectors, overriding
+the corresponding metadata columns.}
+
+\item{assay}{Seurat assay. NULL uses DefaultAssay(object).}
+
+\item{layer}{Expression layer, defaulting to data for Seurat or X for AnnData.
+Select one joined Seurat layer.}
+
+\item{input.scale}{Nonnegative log1p expression or counts. Counts are normalized
+to 10,000 per cell and transformed with log1p.}
+
+\item{reduction}{Seurat reduction or AnnData obsm key used for the tree.
+NULL uses up to 500 variable cluster-average gene profiles.}
+
+\item{tree}{Optional hclust with cluster-ID labels. Otherwise use Pearson
+distance and complete linkage on cluster-average profiles.}
+
+\item{min.pct}{Minimum expressing fraction (0--1) for displaying marker dots.}
+
+\item{expression.cutoff}{Nonnegative expression threshold used to count
+expressing cells, after any counts normalization.}
+
+\item{min.program.genes}{Minimum matched variable genes per program.}
+
+\item{feature.labels, pathway.labels}{Named ID-to-label vectors.
